{
  "name": "Islanded GPU Ramp \u2014 3-Hour Cyclic Load Profile (50\u21921000\u2192500\u21921000\u219250\u21921000\u219250)",
  "description": "This scenario demonstrates GridSignal managing a full-cycle GPU load profile over three hours, with six distinct workload phases separated by idle transition windows. The site starts at a 50-node floor, ramps to 1,000 nodes over 30 minutes, reduces to 500 for a mid-cycle plateau, peaks again at 1,000, drops back to the floor, peaks a final time, and then winds down over the closing 30 minutes. Each ramp and shed phase spreads its job events evenly across its window so generation staging, N-1 coverage, and reserve status evolve gradually rather than stepping all at once. This matters because real AI data centres cycle through training, inference, and idle phases repeatedly within a shift, and operators need to see how GridSignal behaves across the full demand envelope \u2014 not just the initial ramp.",
